[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\fill[gray!35] (0,0) -- (0,1.05) -- (4.2,2.73) -- (4.2,0) -- cycle;
\draw[->] (-0.4,0) -- (5.3,0);
\draw[->] (0,-0.4) -- (0,3.6);
\draw[thick] (0,1.05) -- (4.2,2.73);
\foreach \t in {1,2,3,4,5,6} \draw ({0.7*\t},0.1) -- ({0.7*\t},-0.1) node[below,font=\footnotesize] {$\t$};
\foreach \p/\lab in {0.7/10,1.4/20,2.1/30} \draw (0.1,\p) -- (-0.1,\p) node[left,font=\footnotesize] {$\lab$};
\node[below] at (2.1,-0.85) {Time $t$ (minutes)};
\node[rotate=90] at (-1.4,1.6) {Rate $R$ (litres/min)};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
A tank initially contains $100$ litres of petrol. Petrol flows into it at a rate of $R=15+4t$ litres per minute, for $0\le t\le 6$ minutes.
How much petrol is in the tank after $6$ minutes?

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\fill[gray!35] (-2.2,0) -- plot[domain=-2:2,smooth,variable=\x] ({1.1*\x},{0.17*(16-4*\x*\x)}) -- (2.2,0) -- cycle;
\draw[->] (-3.2,0) -- (3.4,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-0.5) -- (0,3.7) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick,domain=-2:2,smooth,variable=\x] plot ({1.1*\x},{0.17*(16-4*\x*\x)});
\draw (-2.2,0.1) -- (-2.2,-0.1) node[below,font=\footnotesize] {$-2$};
\draw (2.2,0.1) -- (2.2,-0.1) node[below,font=\footnotesize] {$2$};
\draw (0.1,2.72) -- (-0.1,2.72) node[left,font=\footnotesize] {$16$};
\node[below] at (0,-0.85) {$x$ (metres)};
\node at (2.7,3.3) {$y=16-4x^{2}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
The cross-section of a road tunnel is the region between the curve $y=16-4x^{2}$ and the level roadway $y=0$, with $x$ and $y$ measured in metres.
What is the area of the cross-section?

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\fill[gray!35] (0,0) -- plot[domain=0:5,smooth,variable=\x] ({0.8*\x},{2.75*exp(-0.2*\x)}) -- (4.0,0) -- cycle;
\draw[->] (-0.4,0) -- (5.1,0);
\draw[->] (0,-0.4) -- (0,3.6);
\draw[thick,domain=0:5,smooth,variable=\x] plot ({0.8*\x},{2.75*exp(-0.2*\x)});
\foreach \t in {1,2,3,4,5} \draw ({0.8*\t},0.1) -- ({0.8*\t},-0.1) node[below,font=\footnotesize] {$\t$};
\foreach \p/\lab in {0.55/100,1.1/200,1.65/300,2.2/400,2.75/500} \draw (0.1,\p) -- (-0.1,\p) node[left,font=\footnotesize] {$\lab$};
\node[below] at (2.0,-0.85) {Time $t$ (days)};
\node[rotate=90] at (-1.8,1.6) {Rate $R$ (kL/day)};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
A dam initially contains $3000$ kilolitres of water. It loses water at a rate of $R=500e^{-0.2t}$ kilolitres per day, for $0\le t\le 5$ days.
How much water remains after $5$ days, to the nearest kilolitre?

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\fill[gray!35] (0,0) -- plot[domain=0:3.1416,smooth,variable=\x] ({1.2*\x},{2.6*sin(deg(\x))}) -- (3.7699,0) -- cycle;
\draw[->] (-0.5,0) -- (4.8,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-0.5) -- (0,3.5) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick,domain=0:3.1416,smooth,variable=\x] plot ({1.2*\x},{2.6*sin(deg(\x))});
\draw (3.7699,0.1) -- (3.7699,-0.1) node[below,font=\footnotesize] {$\pi$};
\draw (0.1,2.6) -- (-0.1,2.6) node[left,font=\footnotesize] {$4$};
\node[below] at (1.9,-0.9) {$x$ (metres)};
\node at (3.4,3.0) {$y=4\sin x$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
The curved roof of a shelter follows $y=4\sin x$ above the horizontal ceiling $y=0$, for $0\le x\le\pi$, with $x$ and $y$ measured in metres.
What is the area of the end wall between the roof and the ceiling?
